// The value-carrying CRDTs take *values* in `insert`/`set`, but `merge` still takes their own type:
// accepting any value where an element goes must not loosen the type that defines the lattice.
// Merging an `OrSet` with a `GSet` is a static error, exactly as it is for the counters.
// expect: error E0007 at 9:5
// expect: exit 1
use para.{crdt}

a = crdt.orset().insert("A", "x")
b = a.merge(crdt.gset().insert("x"))
echo b.len()
